s":null,"syntax_migration_status":null,"syntax_migration_notes":null,"created_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.215Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.215Z"},{"id":"01a00466-c961-703e-836f-eef2aafa2205","topic_id":"019f9df7-a2a2-7853-96ff-2c02dc5e1f10","prompt":"The first four terms of a sequence are 11, 16, 21 and 26. Find the 9th term and an expression for the nth term.","model_answer":"9th term = 51; Tn = 5n + 6","explanation":"The common difference is 5. Therefore, Tn = 11 + (n - 1)5 = 5n + 6. T9 = 5(9) + 6 = 51.","difficulty":"Easy","metadata":{"diagram_required":false},"diagram_path":null,"question_type":null,"answer_tolerance":null,"accepted_answers":null,"case_sensitive":null,"require_simplified_form":null,"require_units":null,"required_unit":null,"accepted_units":null,"marking_notes":null,"syntax_migration_status":null,"syntax_migration_notes":null,"created_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.224Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.224Z"},{"id":"01a00466-c96a-7fa4-a22d-57c08e185844","topic_id":"019f9df7-a2a2-7941-9e48-3d4dda1f252c","prompt":"A school has 36 students. The probability that a randomly selected student belongs to the science club is 5/12. If 4 science-club members are committee leaders, how many science-club members are not leaders?","model_answer":"11","explanation":"Number of science-club members = (5/12) × 36 = 15. Non-leaders = 15 - 4 = 11.","difficulty":"Easy","metadata":{"diagram_required":false},"diagram_path":null,"question_type":null,"answer_tolerance":null,"accepted_answers":null,"case_sensitive":null,"require_simplified_form":null,"require_units":null,"required_unit":null,"accepted_units":null,"marking_notes":null,"syntax_migration_status":null,"syntax_migration_notes":null,"created_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.234Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.234Z"},{"id":"01a00466-c975-720c-988f-5711c5a08a76","topic_id":"019f9df7-a2a2-7941-9e48-3d4dda1f252c","prompt":"A bag contains 6 red counters, 5 blue counters and 9 green counters. Two counters are selected without replacement. Find the probability that both counters are red.","model_answer":"3/38","explanation":"Total counters = 20. P(both red) = (6/20) × (5/19) = 30/380 = 3/38.","difficulty":"Medium","metadata":{"diagram_required":false},"diagram_path":null,"question_type":null,"answer_tolerance":null,"accepted_answers":null,"case_sensitive":null,"require_simplified_form":null,"require_units":null,"required_unit":null,"accepted_units":null,"marking_notes":null,"syntax_migration_status":null,"syntax_migration_notes":null,"created_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.244Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.244Z"},{"id":"01a00466-c97e-7ead-a93a-c7decf743b02","topic_id":"019f9df7-a2a0-71cf-9863-4d6d67e42e6d","prompt":"A town’s population is 6,240,000 and its land area is 780 km². Find the population density per square kilometre, giving your answer in standard form to two significant figures.","model_answer":"8.0 × 10³ people per km²","explanation":"Population density = 6,240,000 ÷ 780 = 8000 people per km² = 8.0 × 10³ people per km².","difficulty":"Easy","metadata":{"diagram_required":false},"diagram_path":null,"question_type":null,"answer_tolerance":null,"accepted_answers":null,"case_sensitive":null,"require_simplified_form":null,"require_units":null,"required_unit":null,"accepted_units":null,"marking_notes":null,"syntax_migration_status":null,"syntax_migration_notes":null,"created_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.254Z","updated_at":"2026-08-15T07:50:40.254Z"},{"id":"01a00466-c989-7207-9d14-d6b789fbf7e3","topic_id":"019f9df7-a2a2-7839-8287-1e75e9dd37f8","prompt":"A painting was worth 25% more in 2024 than in 2023. In 2025, its value was 20% less than its 2024 value. If its 2025 value was $18,000, find its 2023 value.","model_answer":"$18,000","explanation":"2024 value = 18,000 ÷ 0.8 = 22,500. 2023 value = 22,500 ÷ 1.25 = $18,000.","difficulty":"Medium","metadata":{"diagram_required":false},"diagram_path":null,"question_type":null,"answer_tolerance":null,"accepted_answers":null,"case_sensitiv